      "hash": "2c95651ce531e8c126a55f31a4fe307bef2629804bb3b968416f03ececc549b4"
    },
    {
      "id": "d582c1016f590410340a27c19af167f8762b2049165304de7478ae3ea3b3b460",
      "text": "Conclusion",
      "hash": "89db2ad881f29c18b305a20c8ed7bdffdfde49d633c27a83bd204bf9cfedaba3"
    },
    {
      "id": "cd506b22f046370c648029dd0a063c762ca34f417e191a28a30593478b8e38c7",
      "text": "Up next",
      "hash": "e31da5b25f8b7324861e9aadaf5c503e7fd43e739fa3be17ebe63e999fb13df1"
    },
    {
      "id": "28cef8eb36fecd9765b6228968eab33702c3e39011045911406ab8c9ce0c5757",
      "text": "Related reading",
      "hash": "89c21c36ad5ffbab7b05ced367c46013c8d7b8ddf53a8b9739b7b2545f78abee"
    },
    {
      "id": "dd39a1a4c6093e327947da1a826c683f1ef95278a406ee54235fceab14a9c493",
      "text": "A huge benefit of MCP's design is that you can very easily distribute MCP servers using freely available tools.",
      "hash": "20635b79894dbdf6aa78f71d8b115bae89338d2f2da7b4092d689b891f9288d6"
    },
    {
      "id": "d14d5235cf7110bb6367f672a16e63f7b05912d98fca899f20391cf3df32c4bb",
      "text": "In this example, we're going to take",
      "hash": "aa73635c3038cef7a16b595cfee2e73096c59cc6edfecb8d76dd6201fad12874"
    },
    {
      "id": "4096e94cf46071fcb1f0cf6455ad65c0ca98964758097b851cf83316577bf3c1",
      "text": "our simple MCP server",
      "hash": "7fe060e8f6252292dbfa794d0b8c428d39418cefab3397fac91ff218d7142522"
    },
    {
      "id": "15c730ea6759ac2beb4c9c7cac2e9594cd6881703f8460a8174e43c4d57b4033",
      "text": "and publish it to NPM.",
      "hash": "a5607766b7349a3d51187a6806931834fe09bdc1a92335e9766085dcb47b6c51"
    },
    {
      "id": "88c0504f4fe018dad9d2f5e2697660c05defc95d0cf4cd47c96217316c6c5d3f",
      "text": "Once we've done that, anyone with",
      "hash": "c8204cd1e4e67c6aea541688b97e4393aac842f0ca577441e624d264672e96e3"
    },
    {
      "id": "d6597ca369f5106f5d0a630bec09b2ff001f6e27f851c8e4404db88a2b0da92c",
      "text": "Node",
      "hash": "e93372533f323b2f12783aa3a586135cf421486439c2cdcde47411b78f9839ec"
    },
    {
      "id": "0e51db4b61df738768778d03d628178c36800be949f6457eb355391624e582ff",
      "text": "installed will immediately be able to run our MCP server via",
      "hash": "0e382b9332d8eaef2e7796afc772f1a3c8f5f9762ce2ecf6af443a3072548a78"
    },
    {
      "id": "e204ca922a18011e569ff2815e09eb20aa19a523548d9160b947069cf4aa9acd",
      "text": ". We'll be able to push updates to it, and users will get those updates automatically.",
      "hash": "3e1d9847eea50eac3a028b407e12863bf2d746d40b6d2a1ff5002cf19bd73b7a"
    },
    {
      "id": "f9d645e6d3762585a606e328b6e7e1579e50248f5898097993cadc15e1826e88",
      "text": "We're going to be following recommendations from my previous article on Total TypeScript on",
      "hash": "8fc57658b9becd47f3ef8c662b4426f4422166ee35e263f1ab1ca437beddd38c"
    },
    {
      "id": "504c60b5cc1f0381e2ed0d72a27f88c0c02689048088856e443441f8c7c48081",
      "text": "how to create an NPM package",
      "hash": "cf853625a7c879ac1f2c5a2d9c31a4f58bdeebddb5f3503bc37ed35f624239dd"
    },
    {
      "id": "4ffeec57b7cd60e8ddad47ae838dd13fefe27cd959ec5b6b68f7c36c73192ea4",
      "text": "The way users are going to run our MCP server is by using",
      "hash": "a2659cc3cd6fb6e2b52e7fd574f43bc4531a4d0f3d9b3a086b7ca3fab83a19ce"
    },
    {
      "id": "fccce8be59336f43816dad1e9d84a3e59db84fccd1293e9a082ab262758e27ab",
      "text": ". This is a tool that comes with Node.js that lets users run any package on NPM.",
      "hash": "a3c43486076052812fc441854a67dce712307ade2bfaf0667b95d27880a2d2a5"
    },
    {
      "id": "438c51d03343bc502db5f63b152d5cad0f9087d35986e2e39f72cf6b9a0003c3",
      "text": "They'll be running this command:",
      "hash": "481baad2d520dd996edd40cfbc64652346b18638ba0aef624de841ef980665af"
    },
    {
      "id": "94e01f868bd5f71e003f35d7157a33cf8a9d6c7928803dcdff9bd9e5146cba6b",
      "text": "This will:",
      "hash": "3f2cfbc950d5bec695c7f0e719d65abba8f2d9b6d876b6385ec5222731ac34f3"
    },
    {
      "id": "2d8d5ad59116f04d103abb656ff05fbca05786999d04b3b455750025b386bd19",
      "text": "Download the latest version of our package to a global cache (using the",
      "hash": "0c5c2351c57ff3b128e7a680806c7adfbc5efc2c9cf908a7ad06d27932de2c89"
    },
    {
      "id": "eee3132d5cd3e4c0735f70a884f59756ec8692bf4492f377fbe62993639abb3d",
      "text": "tag)",
      "hash": "ec8e232f92ac4ddf9e41ef6c19ecb39bec57eb20c04e151c973d2d5a54e2a083"
    },
    {
      "id": "afe768d70bb0614c791b2090393d19fc8a832c68316e4bf1252a485cbfd95cb4",
      "text": "Ignore the confirmation message that usually appears when running a package for the first time (using the",
      "hash": "ca6d5981f9e9234a1c8871ab84bf137802aaefd088ff4bb8fc5acf68860b01ca"
    },
    {
      "id": "71bd9c5e4a446572c499ff01b5d51af93a2f207fc1196e8fd8f5128369167ad3",
      "text": "flag).",
      "hash": "e23be3049f7aa6c0e5a87da38715a57605112cfa8886eb510a80cf631d3c84b0"
    },
    {
      "id": "3fe2cf1e081079e27300fb27de19d9391d88a656506e86b920e5fb5efd3de509",
      "text": "Run a file referenced inside that package's",
      "hash": "4fcb641d0a1ad630fbd75a078f7782de7a51762a15b7d0e12df3f235ef94f140"
    },
    {
      "id": "e5b073e9c7a158936f8b3780fcd03e3ad777dc076e3fb117e436e27ee52c2249",
      "text": "So, it's a way of running a package without having to install it.",
      "hash": "a4cd021ec0e77b00f47e9f75655e387ee621db4c371f47e0ff85778a208b8953"
    },
    {
      "id": "f96d94ad38948ba4b88b26ad4d9eb198fbacb5071ee049246dd0afaa7cbc4212",
      "text": "It's worth noting that this is not without its dangers. If you're running a package from an untrusted source, you should always check the source code first.",
      "hash": "42e6ee362f46f3185e8c7bd00e45c18c42fee46e2b38e54d803cacf42895e4b4"
    },
    {
      "id": "2c2c11a1404ade7a8e2df20a144007f1b031033ca553bb9c467bfdb45eb7ce26",
      "text": "Go deeper:",
      "hash": "15ad3d88c6733d9b257c322d3afecc9bce2b18558171007db87598c118ca17f9"
    },
    {
      "id": "f74a8faf330c3a3c2cd0a29a05a4504525ef0fcdf0391c27aa501841f3f46f04",
      "text": "join the waitlist for AI Coding for Real Engineers",
      "hash": "16c3492a8464a0859c944e287a9d433e9a2635f22a6bd8aad59f88c3e80ab732"
    },
    {
      "id": "faa7587fbea474f569ed2aa1d27772b6b21f5297b9d86ce6e4dcbb92b5cad489",
      "text": "The server and the transport will sit in a single file called",
      "hash": "54be82ef19a05a51399c50fe9a629b5014d6c4d06310251969f55b2d1a43afc8"
    },
    {
      "id": "c1be6ffd42fb22297f3d997dab850bebbbb7c7a51d5a53419c493087425dfeeb",
      "text": ". This is the file that will be executed when the user runs our server.",
      "hash": "d30846c1872a02128f66bded816d7b25dc28704dc3137e551bc1c400ef6436c4"
    },
    {
      "id": "f3fa170b37a9bfad1ee5b6c9d8888ed7fd1431e045c6a50e2fc1db2c4123e00d",
      "text": "We're going to add a single line to the top of this file: a shebang.",
      "hash": "9b4f7a930e3f39f565454c8af05221e281929b55e28d3a0cba2cb2043c1bcda9"
    },
    {
      "id": "be0e8b7034624fe37532ea342cf8f1d045334408fbbcf9250fafb1f4c3b507d2",
      "text": "This is a special line that tells the operating system how to run the file. In this case, we're telling it to run the file using Node.js.",
      "hash": "fb4b52b3b11cdd2013a1ebbf492c22c3f2cf165c9ae877e47dc7b676c2b9f61f"
    },
    {
      "id": "724810c396c65b84b13ea5bd9459db263db78f200b5a77fe92fcb5db5009d073",
      "text": "We'll need a",
      "hash": "bad689c65b5af5846c5ab5626ea472e78d45bcbcf82b1c359f93b01672c332ed"
    },
    {
      "id": "dfdcc2494698c1f44960d967def41c915fe4f8108380afc876e38b85fbd8d044",
      "text": "file to describe our package. Here's what it looks like:",
      "hash": "fb09c2fd63e83246470a32305bef887d681b57d1bec824c3d94c7cee27a1d369"
    },
    {
      "id": "60b7dc4d1dfe40f804d6d380521e83b795f68072a23e5a2af209456f897b0930",
      "text": "Note that the comments will need to be deleted if you copy/paste this into your own",
      "hash": "80166f5cd68eb0c92a30a5d6b58eca7f552e56ee39b0aa271969119fc6716020"
    },
    {
      "id": "c1bc7c6fcb71e9bd07292cd2573b5c2f66a7b523a8571be588c5364b94ff6278",
      "text": "The most important part of this file is the",
      "hash": "f7a17452ff8c119ff63055d51e9d93f9faf9b872cac9ecec3cefa4d737406119"
    },
    {
      "id": "6ce977f77040a8b7264e995023f714a91a73b111c0140a798670de01b2857e16",
      "text": "field. This tells",
      "hash": "06b834de63b8971527528183ac6d7fe5fd60d863b13b3a354a02d7563f05c431"
    },
    {
      "id": "22fa83df37cfceb494dcb67cc2aaa387ea5609f9163de99ec4f3c788dc72e97c",
      "text": "which file to run when executing your MCP server. The details for how this logic works is described",
      "hash": "1721f15650baae96c75d7965cfeba9273ca1925e52d6ae0bdde1e42eac3d2136"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8f06771b77b008af62d27c5f2451d0b9f1bf2378ff31d77e2b1d9093171738c",
      "text": ". The important quote is:",
      "hash": "b8048d93bc626cc62ec30d7d3cb45abf5205e7bbe74ce3703c008a9b30eec00c"
    },
    {
      "id": "7c80e474ec86353999d5b1c04ac724e5265a883d6f40c0a056591f189b155242",
      "text": "If the package has a single entry in its",
      "hash": "28f28ec73ff19fa15733d7d57606881fcd22d7122722c658a0d7c00c49d28fdd"
    },
    {
      "id": "ed8b9709c322141d18472ba187bee420003c682ee8d361cb250842f62d0b94ea",
      "text": "field in",
      "hash": "71732a2c2f014c3b7a6f677155f79a4626593e987978a18de2c1133f357d5935"
    },
    {
      "id": "169163a648f3fadd2ae728b744c675b4432756b20e934cf70ec558f890c05da9",
      "text": "[...] then that command will be used.",
      "hash": "6110b177077749fa1bd896ef65ccad59915b3e115d5004bd91b291faf09ae29a"
    },
    {
      "id": "0ba369f4312b733f99ccc7ddaccc4484b028eb28dfc2e3e96a145f8536fd30ac",
      "text": "So, having a single entry in the",
      "hash": "f6442b80dcd55dc6dda86cbf78fcba5aa693a54d883fc0c6832be1435e3cc381"
    },
    {
      "id": "7f92b1acff2e40630df7841e7791b208e2b897f7d5befe117fba8cadc73257ca",
      "text": "field, no matter what its name is, means that",
      "hash": "f91d3d18b68703c906fbe32ca74ace21254ba9c58ff68d451f1c1397f67f640e"
    },
    {
      "id": "b792755793bc8405b5748ba55671bc404a5431c334d57e70a4aa17e6a6ae9e25",
      "text": "will run that file. In our case, that will be",
      "hash": "253c4ab257fcf7cdeba8954a613f4092af7d14c6927283fc453f5495c88e7b64"
    },
    {
      "id": "52c7847c49b7a9dd00ba29919a1dd95ef5cadcd49792a80c19e6581172d49fff",
      "text": "The file we're going to run is",
      "hash": "f88036d497f20b969a26c4674d386f4d4889b0c347824dd4081caa483fbb4995"
    },
    {
      "id": "78cdd5fcce181634252eff411bb7257e453c38cdcbc8d6e41880b611400d022e",
      "text": ". This is the file that will be built by TypeScript.",
      "hash": "40509adca00c4a4055c3aef3c16c2e94b84b8b9a8e3ef2cb9e92146ac82959ab"
    },
    {
      "id": "8337688cefb6f7ada78d804ba9118467bea0094585c1350317ea9ff3f03479ae",
      "text": "TypeScript is going to be responsible for turning our",
      "hash": "575ffc5ffd53a811d207f416b21bc976d6a0d80d2008921d5c09518b95d32140"
    },
    {
      "id": "dce12b745cb6a870f54b57bc30a827f6fae7f4a09d737a926ccf7b5bb468f3bd",
      "text": "file into a file that Node can run - a",
      "hash": "d2b472d90a50a245f88f0ff653980bf4323a7d88311953fd6fc329f7744dc5f4"
    },
    {
      "id": "6e4b7893a7a9176d8c77a6b1d11799a184fed997406db32bc88623d90fd9c385",
      "text": "file.",
      "hash": "eb36be6c06717c3b88700bdc0678576b33b6b4ef76de644a43b56023e9e77cb0"
    },
    {
      "id": "20444d3fc18b8f5c9184e7b16899d9638ea6dbb4a6e76736eb0f7b630246be0f",
      "text": "We'll start by adding a",
      "hash": "8e170beffd09d71a040489809e56a6b797fee2e8789de52a8c773319f3beef93"
    },
    {
      "id": "4673a8f2a6a901e9952e0eb6b67213fb77d5fdd01b96f142f6877ecb72943b3f",
      "text": "file:",
      "hash": "430473329df5ca205e93d09d202c021d973044142fe20fc4abf555135c405c44"
    },
    {
      "id": "a27b0d5afb21bf62a2ee95423c9845049f6340f10a2b5cfcfd4acbe1ec4451f2",
      "text": "This will tell typescript how to build our project. The most important part is the",
      "hash": "d5f70c3b7d4d1902359c4a998c137d6e56742f05f2156a29ae0a87c38ae91b9d"
    },
    {
      "id": "e819584232e698c0c0aeb70dea6c01e57fa1da67e119a14bea8842c7e3fb45b1",
      "text": "field. This tells TypeScript where to put the built files. It means that",
      "hash": "d9a58bd3d2c7d0c9f33beebc6ea07241282afd8be741b0ce21663aa241b94305"
    },
    {
      "id": "6806c1b4be87c1df1254b6a29b4c8aaa5237c319aac3cf944e6bef619409f4fc",
      "text": "will turn into",
      "hash": "745304d0ed342bb6bae9e5cf745cbc90712d5304c54c2619d9a1fa8ac732c276"
    },
    {
      "id": "1c36d8290571e36b52e5aa4a67f1cc3664264beddf18953a80afe9f902c57224",
      "text": "To publish our package, we'll need to run the following command:",
      "hash": "3ca42bcc2be22ae6f32b9f3aded5df68e80a23b96236a2664b4db9bf93083ac4"
    },
    {
      "id": "edf915d68a93ed49e2ff04b64e1edf5cf277d78fdfbeaf886c7cea8a040bccfb",
      "text": "This will publish our package to NPM. The",
      "hash": "7bba3e91463b81bf3ea002181c2d9b0ade098f5c2878f7354a6af0fafcd6abdc"
    },
    {
      "id": "4a67802a3dcecbb3d6893f23aadee4cc55d46f3d4580cf8a8cbcdc3a2af701f2",
      "text": "flag means that anyone can install it.",
      "hash": "e63a90226223968d5419a1e7a5fe372b461c4bc93d14d4c50ba6c650a036ef0f"
    },
    {
      "id": "e82d347b1ec3fd515ac181c0b2959128b9615fae752bee49bd81afb17dee8780",
      "text": "You may get one of several errors:",
      "hash": "59dce68156485ca228e9d3bcc3f98b1da97cb0432c7877f7a6226b30e3225ea4"
    },
    {
      "id": "3990b4ae18b2fa741674db0180e01b274971e5f67d50d25baae5b64250f71433",
      "text": "If you haven't logged in, you'll need to run",
      "hash": "dadfa21ee5dfda0a25502ab6b5f07be718c9c142f0e2ce02df4086d7cc506120"
    },
    {
      "id": "446c3ea8871bfe89a090de3641eba6a9cbb9cfe790aae1b08366ba49ab19e82a",
      "text": "first.",
      "hash": "0eac7d776c9029669c4164ab8063f8ffee803f453c0cf2743d36726d8288dc8c"
    },
    {
      "id": "2bd19183d1d1de493fb725055a404d18343d3938aa95d9de2fa62d3e11a314b4",
      "text": "If your package name is already taken, you'll need to change it.",
      "hash": "8db7994a5440ac272bd9f0a931087ec877ab0f37ff62e64c7351173341c30d4e"
    },
    {
      "id": "3ec1a96ca4685636d0845e4bedb68c8fa71ca6d0d9a047606489c82caa5842f7",
      "text": "But once you've worked through them, your package will be published!",
      "hash": "808fb098d43c006fb82fa3db0057033512582c7faf019b18927c7b7c16de40f4"
    },
    {
      "id": "76fd7fb100d9452b6ff2569d3886c9a8d6828c808844d5247dbe72786801f29a",
      "text": "You can test it out by running the following command:",
      "hash": "4f0ffbd7e32a27cb14e3f42c8e497b8d65e27a35f66af54f78d344bed25b8ee3"
    },
    {
      "id": "c9429cc7746a3a5aa971b89730ebc99e05a2cdc923cfe4cd6c98f9965b7b5f59",
      "text": "This will run the latest version of your package. You can also run a specific version by changing",
      "hash": "b3ca64bdc50a4aa6dc179b3625db9e2be96723255d786cc0ffa1cd7d605166dc"
    },
    {
      "id": "96d532ea80149712d15ec3f6c9e3b389f4e4bc0d4a67d98bdbe49ca3a2c7aa75",
      "text": "or whatever version you want to run.",
      "hash": "9d7613b4163145cc682e2923a7225e62ad966208c8d4f101db65d1ba0d8ec828"
    },
    {
      "id": "4a5dc7fdfcf6eb19a5ed7b842c2a14849f45c35c4812637ad83530a228fa00a2",
      "text": "Oddly, you won't see anything in the terminal. This is because the server is monitoring stdin for commands.",
      "hash": "343833585f9e0bd3d310661d29177d6d9de6aef03db341382fbce661df96ed3e"
    },
    {
      "id": "52772d63e86ab68d25136aab255d8577da248ee186930ec37fd2cd70bb1bc18b",
      "text": "You can try connecting it to a MCP server like Cursor, and asking it for the weather in your city.",
      "hash": "4027eb05633e098960ce279d52ab8b69399000fbbd10d7c60fff409b65a17e4e"
    },
    {
      "id": "4ed46edb8e6e47d03251855c051644b354a9d46cae430c74b131192bba471e84",
      "text": "In this article, we've seen how easy it is to publish an MCP server to NPM. This means that anyone with Node.js installed can run your server with a single command.",
      "hash": "870522dcc7008ed7f4ee1c56788f66e0eb0cbc7335b713fb4d01ad033e120f01"
    },
    {
      "id": "ccfa0662ed106462441c9c4861ad367496004ea3d4b1b3361b45fcfd5d23b05e",
      "text": "This is a really powerful way of distributing your MCP servers to anyone who wants to use them.",
      "hash": "b2e23c97039b90eeecf1d1d1561d06b48538aaff6eba7b3f7b97681445e06d35"
    },
    {
      "id": "0350dfdb73254ae4c01bfbf713094616338a0a008af3f67379bda967c466a587",
      "text": "Share on X",
      "hash": "78d21bbf6b047944ec42890d28e151c61dbab35213fc65cc7be70c0c19c24407"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0d12631dcc9d63c52ad36901fb0699460362f71ca0ac2ef8e8f4b0870a28a2e",
      "text": "Share on Bluesky",
      "hash": "08863b88a05c60410c38c4caec5bc72535b0f01793ce6cee9171b6358b2c11da"
    },
    {
      "id": "ee0427eace911e3231f15d2fbedf412f2f13ee25dedc6b316287ed6c49075cbc",
      "text": "Share on LinkedIn",
      "hash": "ab87c050148bd1d372e3ec3483a606127a7a1faec0f1ca5543bc3465d84fe6c9"
    },
    {
      "id": "8a9f9f3d943477b4de051db5da34f4a9300697855664e28cfd15fff48231657c",
      "text": "Copy URL",
      "hash": "b26d1037f1c2da31a0296d915982f12049f91bfedb998b105ce967b73a796699"
    },
    {
      "id": "84bdaddd4c5a77cd4b7984b05a0d48cb77ef7e901f96fb271a8fa0b463ac0128",
      "text": "Previous",
      "hash": "a57b08a480b822a0a572b993391c292ede593bf8000b406675b180bbb16260fa"
    },
    {
